  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 3,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.447,
            0.97,
            0.552,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.085,
            0.899,
            0.135
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note that the metal in the above reactions displaces hydrogen atoms from the acids as hydrogen gas and forms a compound called a salt. Thus, the reaction of a metal with an acid can be summarised as –",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.141,
            0.63,
            0.158
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Acid + Metal → Salt + Hydrogen gas",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.165,
            0.899,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you now write the equations for the reactions you have observed?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.202,
            0.476,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 2.4"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.309,
            0.239,
            0.818,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Place a few pieces of granulated zinc metal in a test tube.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.31,
            0.256,
            0.869,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Add 2 mL of sodium hydroxide solution and warm the contents of the test tube.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.309,
            0.284,
            0.869,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Repeat the rest of the steps as in Activity 2.3 and record your observations.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.336,
            0.79,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The reaction that takes place can be written as follows.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.36,
            0.659,
            0.397
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} 2NaOH(aq)  +  Zn(s)  \\rightarrow  Na _2 ZnO _2 (s)  +  H _2 (g)  \\\\ (SOdim zincate) \\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.412,
            0.897,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You find again that hydrogen is formed in the reaction. However, such reactions are not possible with all metals.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.275,
            0.46,
            0.761,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.1.3 How do Metal Carbonates and Metal Hydrogencarbonates React with Acids?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.078,
            0.506,
            0.497,
            0.698
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 12,
              "bbox": [
                0.078,
                0.506,
                0.497,
                0.698
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_image_12.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.075,
                0.702,
                0.168,
                0.717
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Figure 2.2"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.075,
                0.717,
                0.287,
                0.758
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Passing carbon dioxide gas through calcium hydroxide solution"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.557,
            0.507,
            0.711,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 2.5"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.559,
            0.541,
            0.876,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take two test tubes, label them as A and B.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.571,
            0.874,
            0.629
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take about 0.5 g of sodium carbonate",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{(Na_{2}CO_{3})}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "in test tube A and about",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 . 5 ~ \\mathrm { g }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "of sodium hydrogencarbonate",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( \\mathrm { N a H C O } _ { 3 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "in test tube B.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.541,
            0.629,
            0.873,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Add about 2 mL of dilute HCl to both the test tubes.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.541,
            0.658,
            0.756,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What do you observe?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.54,
            0.673,
            0.875,
            0.733
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pass the gas produced in each case through lime water (calcium hydroxide solution) as shown in Fig. 2.2 and record your observations.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.753,
            0.845,
            0.77
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The reactions occurring in the above Activity are written as –",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.776,
            0.894,
            0.794
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Test tube A: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{Na_{2}CO_{3}(s)+2HCl(aq)\\rightarrow 2NaCl(aq)+H_{2}O(l)+CO_{2}(}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(g)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.799,
            0.879,
            0.817
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Test tube B: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{NaHCO_{3}(s)+HCl(aq)\\rightarrow NaCl(aq)+H_{2}O(l)+CO_{2}(g)}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.822,
            0.864,
            0.84
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "On passing the carbon dioxide gas evolved through lime water,",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.421,
            0.845,
            0.812,
            0.883
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_25.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} & Ca(OH) _2 (aq)  +  CO _2 (g)  \\rightarrow  CaCO _3 (s)  +  H _2 O(l) \\\\ &\\begin{aligned} (Line water)  \\quad & (white reweighted)  \\end{aligned}\\\\ \\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
